NOTE ON THIRD-PARTY DATA — THE MIT LICENSE ABOVE COVERS THE SOURCE CODE ONLY.

This repository bundles **no datasets**. Every record shown on the globe is
fetched at runtime from a third-party provider and remains subject to that
provider's own licence and terms of use. The MIT grant does not extend to any
of it.

Per-source licences, attribution strings and usage limits are listed in
DATA_SOURCES.md and are surfaced in the running application's Attribution
panel. If you fork this project, review those terms before redistributing or
using it commercially — several providers restrict commercial use or require
you to supply your own credentials.

Two deliberate omissions, made because their terms do not fit a permissively
licensed project:

  - TeleGeography's submarine cable map is CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 (NonCommercial).
    It is not bundled and not fetched. Submarine cables are therefore absent
    from this project by design.
  - No imagery, video or 3D model from any third-party source is bundled.

Not authoritative. Data shown here comes from public feeds of varying latency
and accuracy, some of which are advisory products published on a delay. This
tool is for situational awareness and curiosity. It is not suitable for
navigation, emergency response, or any safety-critical decision.
